{number: 90}
{title: My Faith Looks Up to Thee}
{key: Eb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Eb] My faith looks up to Thee,
[Ab] Thou Lamb of [Bb7] Calva-[Eb] ry,
Savior di-[Bb7] vine:
Now [Eb] hear me while I pray,
Take [Ab] all my [Bb7] guilt a-[Eb] way,
O [Ab] let me from this day
Be [Bb7] wholly [Eb] Thine!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Eb] May Thy rich grace impart
[Ab] Strength to my [Bb7] fainting [Eb] heart,
My zeal in-[Bb7] spire;
As [Eb] Thou hast died for me,
O [Ab] may my [Bb7] love to [Eb] Thee
Pure, [Ab] warm, and changeless be,
A [Bb7] living [Eb] fire!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Eb] While life's dark maze I tread,
[Ab] And griefs a-[Bb7] round me [Eb] spread,
Be Thou my [Bb7] Guide;
Bid [Eb] darkness turn to day,
Wipe [Ab] sorrow's [Bb7] tears a-[Eb] way,
Nor [Ab] let me ever stray
From [Bb7] Thee a-[Eb] side.
{end_of_verse}
